| `scripts/exit_codes.sh` | The shell twin of `scripts/exit_codes.py`, generated from its enum: an `EXIT_<NAME>` variable per member, `exit_fail` for the three-part failure line and `exit_passthrough` for a wrapped tool's status. | `. scripts/exit_codes.sh` | none | Never edited by hand: `make exit-codes-sh` writes it. Not judged by the shell linter, formatter or test runner, and needing no `shell.excluded_paths` entry, because `scripts/shell_gate.py` `HELPER_SH` names it: `make check-exit-codes` and `tests/unit/scripts/test_exit_code_table.py` judge it. | [limits-and-troubleshooting.md](../guides/limits-and-troubleshooting.md) | always |
